<title>GERMANY: German inland gasoil weaker amid strong competitio.</title>
<headline>German inland gasoil weaker amid strong competitio.</headline>
<text>
<p>(DLR/DM=1.7005)   DM/100 LTRS     DLRS/100 LTRS   LAST DM</p>
<p> HAMBURG	     34.10/34.60     20.05/20.34   34.20/34.70</p>
<p> BREMEN		34.10/34.60     20.05/20.34   34.20/34.70</p>
<p> DUISBURG	    33.80/34.30     19.87/20.17   34.20/34.70</p>
<p> FRANKFURT	   34.50/35.00     20.28/20.58   34.50/35.00</p>
<p> KARLSRUHE	   34.50/35.00     20.28/20.58   34.50/35.00</p>
<p> INGOLSTADT	  35.50/36.00     20.87/21.17   35.60/36.00</p>
<p>German inland gas oil prices were marked slightly lower as thin demand stirred strong competition for business. Traders said weaker Rotterdam barge and international futures markets were helping importers remain competitive as mild weather limited demand.</p>
<p>London Newsroom +44 171 542 7456</p>
